  "description": "PUVYOW crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group C m c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C136 H108 Gd6 N14 O48 Zn6. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 10 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 10 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 10 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 10 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 10 O neighbors; Zn4 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Zn5 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 10 O neighbors; Zn6 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.373-3.935 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.06-109.14°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C136H108Gd6N14O48Zn6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
